{
  "title": "About Transaction Plugin",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "bc4430b0d4132ebd",
      "text": "The Transaction plugin draws the `transaction` item of a **Time Transaction** page: the record of one piece of timebank work, as data a ledger can read. Each line is one fact; any other line is a note."
    },
    {
      "type": "transaction",
      "id": "0cc458b90e87661e",
      "text": "GIVER: [https://alice.wiki/view/alices-ledger Alice's Ledger]\nRECEIVER: [https://david.wiki/view/davids-ledger David's Ledger]\nHOURS: 1 hour\nDATE: 3 September 2026\nWHAT: Repairs\nSOURCE: hand\nPlaned the shed door and re-hung the gate."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": "62c7c41e8690ad03",
      "text": "CAPTION The lines of a transaction item\n\n| Line | Example | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| GIVER: | [https://alice.wiki/view/alices-ledger Alice's Ledger] | The ledger of whoever did the work |\n| RECEIVER: | [https://david.wiki/view/davids-ledger David's Ledger] | The ledger of whoever it was for |\n| HOURS: | 1 hour \u00b7 90 minutes \u00b7 1.5h | How long |\n| DATE: | 3 September 2026 | When |\n| WHAT: | Repairs | The ledger label; the page title when absent |\n| SOURCE: | chat message \u00b7 audio note \u00b7 hand | Where the record came from |"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "9f55be5e4d480be7",
      "text": "Name both ledgers by external link, so the page means the same on every site it is forked to. The item adds the class `transaction-source` and a `transactionData()` function to its element, the way map and calendar items expose their data, so a timebank ledger with a `LINEUP` line to its right pulls the entry it implies. Double-click to edit."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "adc8a41fc19f4a47",
      "text": "# One Package, Two Types\nWhy this package is tiny"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "ae1187708df3cc2a",
      "text": "wiki-server serves one item type per plugin package, from `/plugins/<type>/<type>.js`. This package's client file only imports `/plugins/timebank/timebank.js` \u2014 the same module the wiki loads for timebank items, so it runs once \u2014 and registers its transaction plugin as `window.plugins.transaction`. All the code, and its tests, live in wiki-plugin-timebank; install both."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "04d27fff86067296",
      "text": "# One Page, Many Occasions\n> Recurring work, one transaction item each time."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "ed0e282646e4aafd",
      "text": "Name the page for the work and the person \u2014 Childcare for David \u2014 never the date. Beside each transaction item put a date item holding the recorded day (`2026-09-10 Childcare for David`), so the page is a time-located event for the Timeline and Calendar plugins. When the same work is done again for the same person, add another date item and transaction item to the same page: each is an occasion, identified by the page plus the item. Ledgers pull and match each occasion on its own, by its date."
    },
    {
      "type": "date",
      "id": "1880b26d54e0058c",
      "text": "2026-09-10 Childcare for David"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "c3db3804b1d25459",
      "text": "# See\n\n- [[About TimeBank Plugin]] \u2014 ledgers, LINEUP, the badge and the Ledger Verification Tool\n- [[Time Transaction]] \u2014 what a transaction page is, where a site has one"
    }
  ],
